<title>SOUTH KOREA: Ssangyong in Jordan car export venture.</title>
<headline>Ssangyong in Jordan car export venture.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Ssangyong Motor Co, a unit of Ssangyong Group, said on Monday it has agreed to provide completely knocked down (CKD) kit vehicles to Jordan's Middle East Complex PLC.</p>
<p>Ssangyong said in a statement it would deliver kit parts of 1,000 its four-wheel drive Musso and Korando models in 1997. The number is expected to increase to 2,500 in 1998 and to more than 4,000 units annually from 2000, it said.</p>
<p>Middle East Complex will assemble the kit and sell the cars in Jordan, it said. The value of the deal was not disclosed.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
</text>
